-- title:
--   Join of two comultiplication-stable R-subalgebras
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $K$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $A$ a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $K$ together with an $R$-algebra structure compatible with that of $K$ (scalar tower $R \to K \to A$). Let $S, S'$ be $R$-subalgebras of $A$. For an $R$-subalgebra $T \subseteq A$ write $\rho_T : T \otimes_R T \to A \otimes_K A$ for the $R$-algebra map obtained from the pair of inclusions $t \mapsto t \otimes_K 1$ and $t \mapsto 1 \otimes_K t$ (the `Algebra.TensorProduct.productMap` of `includeLeft` and `includeRight` precomposed with the inclusion of $T$, viewed $R$-linearly), so that $\rho_T(t \otimes_R t') = t \otimes_K t'$; its range is an $R$-subalgebra of $A \otimes_K A$. Assume that the comultiplication $\Delta =$ `Coalgebra.comul` over $K$ carries every element of $S$ into the range of $\rho_S$, and every element of $S'$ into the range of $\rho_{S'}$. The conclusion is that for every $x$ in the join $S \sqcup S'$ of the two subalgebras, $\Delta x$ lies in the range of $\rho_{S \sqcup S'}$.
--
--   This is the comultiplication clause in the statement that the $R$-subalgebra generated by two Hopf orders of a $K$-Hopf algebra $A$ is again stable under comultiplication, as in Raynaud's treatment of prolongations of finite flat group schemes. It is used in the construction of a greatest Hopf order ([`HopfOrder.exists_isGreatest`](thm.html#HopfOrder.exists_isGreatest)) and in the uniqueness/base-change statement [`HopfAlgebra.existsUnique_bialgHom_baseChange_eq_of_pow_eq_one`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.existsUnique_bialgHom_baseChange_eq_of_pow_eq_one).
